Check the possible pairs:

- Mean of \(\frac{7}{10}\) and \(\frac{4}{5}\):
\[
\frac{\frac{7}{10}+\frac{4}{5}}{2}
= \frac{\frac{7}{10}+\frac{8}{10}}{2}
= \frac{\frac{15}{10}}{2}
= \frac{15}{20}
= \frac{3}{4}
\]

So \(\frac{3}{4}\) is the arithmetic mean of \(\frac{7}{10}\) and \(\frac{4}{5}\).

The answer is \(\frac{3}{4}\).
